# Git author — benndip only

All commits in this repository must be made as:

- **Name:** `benndip`
- **Email:** `obentabiayuk1@gmail.com`

## Rules

- Set both author and committer to benndip / obentabiayuk1@gmail.com on every commit.
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by` for other agents, or any multi-author trailer.
- Do **not** attribute commits to Cursor, Copilot, Claude, Composer, or any AI assistant.
- Prefer a single-author commit message with no trailers unless the user explicitly asks for one.
- After every commit, verify `git log -1` has **no** `Co-authored-by` line. If Cursor injected one, rewrite that unpushed commit with `git commit-tree` (same tree/parent, clean message) so the trailer is removed. Do not leave AI co-author trailers in history.

## Example

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=benndip \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=obentabiayuk1@gmail.com \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=benndip \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=obentabiayuk1@gmail.com \
git commit -m "Your message here."

# If Co-authored-by appears, strip it before push:
TREE=$(git rev-parse 'HEAD^{tree}')
PARENT=$(git rev-parse 'HEAD^')
NEW=$(printf '%s\n' "Your message here." | \
  GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=benndip GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=obentabiayuk1@gmail.com \
  GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=benndip GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=obentabiayuk1@gmail.com \
  git commit-tree "$TREE" -p "$PARENT")
git reset --soft "$NEW"
```
